  - §4 bootstrap: `engine_server.rs` (← engine.rs by `git mv`: spawn, dispatch, the legacy ghost block until Phase 7), `engine_message.rs` (← `types::EngineMsg`), `engine_inbox.rs` (implements `RuntimeEventSource`), `channel_completion_engine.rs` (+ `start_completion_engine`, the starter the pty receives);
  - §4 event table: header "Event (`EngineMessage`)"; the `Complete` row also gives error replies the local ghost; the idle row reads `completion::ProgressGenerators → ghost_text::SuggestLocalGhostText → reply if changed` (Q15). Write the rows so Phase 7.10 can edit them in place (prep7 K10);
  - §5 Phase 6: "(done: [research](hexagonal-refactor/phase-6-completion.md))" and a "Done at `<registration commit>`" paragraph in the style of Phases 4-5: completion registered, the four legacy files gone (engine.rs moved to bootstrap/engine_server.rs), gate green (N passed), 28 steps in six runs, see the Phase 6 notes;
  - §5 Phase 7 step 4: "Replace the three legacy ghost touchpoints of `engine_server.rs` (`local_ghost_text`, `request_llm_ghost_text`, `clear_ghost_text_cache`) with ghost_text's use cases. Delete `inline.rs`.";
  - §5 Phase 11 step 1: drop the sentence about the test-only `Parser::load_spec`, which went with its last caller in 6.3d;
  - §9: add "Phase 6 notes" after the Phase 5 notes, in their shape: an intro naming the decisions and the deviations of phase-6-completion.md and the 28 steps; bold-labelled bullets that cover every deviation and every numbered Phase 6 note of the phase doc; the open questions' defaults that were applied; a **History** bullet (every commit subject over 72 characters, and any subject the RTK hook rewrote); and a **Hand-offs** bullet for Phases 7, 8, 9 and 11 from "Hand-off notes for later phases". In the same notes, close each Phase 6 item of the Phase 5 notes' hand-offs, saying where it landed or which decision amended it (no `resolve_script`, Q9; the inbox in its own file, Q13; the D6 split of `session_update_refreshes_first_token_items` and `parser_over` replaced by `spec_repository_over` in 6.5c, when the engine tests moved to `build_completion_module`, Q19). The Phase 5 notes' own Phase 11 line ("`Parser::load_spec` goes with the parser in Phase 6") is history: leave it.
- docs/ubiquitous-language.md:
  - completion: add `CommandLineParser`, `ParseContext`, `ArgvState`, `CompletionError`, `CompletionNotice`, `GeneratorSlotView`, `GeneratorOutcome`, `GeneratorCommand`, `GeneratorRunner`, `GeneratorTriggerPolicy`, `CompletionRequestPolicy`, `CompletionResultBuilder`, `ServedRequest`, `RecencyRepository`, `DirectoryLister`, `ExecutableCatalog`;
  - edits: `AliasTable` (a type alias of the std map), `GeneratorKey` (newtype; `for_arg`; the argument key shares its hash), `CompletionRequest` (shell, cwd as a path), `CompletionSession` (+ settings, served request, parse-prefix cache, recency, first-token cache), `ParsePrefixCache` (wholesale clear at 1000; keeps the first-token spec), `GeneratorRun` / `GeneratorStep` (replaces `engine::{Run, Step}` only, since `GeneratorOutcome` now replaces `engine::Outcome`; a run returns `GeneratorCommand`s);
  - terminal_session: add `CompletionEngine` (Port);
  - "host / pump": `EngineInbox` (bootstrap/engine_inbox.rs) implements `RuntimeEventSource`; `ProgressGeneratorsUseCase` + `GeneratorRunner`. Name `EngineServer`, `EngineMessage` and `ChannelCompletionEngine` in prose there; there is no bootstrap section;
  - "cache": add only the parse-prefix cache's home (`CompletionSession`); the first-token cache is already there.
  Keep the table format. Keep out every name the phase doc lists as not in the glossary.
- docs/hexagonal-refactor/README.md:
  - the status table: Phase 6 done, its commit range (`phase6-start` at ff2db5a .. the registration commit), run in six runs; "7-11 not started";
  - the gate paragraph under it, written as Phase 5's: the end commit, tests passed/failed/ignored, clippy 3 (budget 3), golden identical, MISSING 0, CHANGED against ef807c1 and against `phase6-start` (each in the phase's "Test moves" table), DUPLICATE 0;
  - the REGISTERED_MODULES line;
  - "Files here": phase-6-completion.md and phase-6-completion.args.json.
- docs/hexagonal-refactor/phase-6-completion.md: its Status line becomes **done** at the registration commit, with the range and the gate numbers, pointing at the plan's "Phase 6 notes" (where they differ from the briefs, the notes win), as phase-5-specs.md does.

6. Final checks (report each result):
- the full gate;
- testlock against phase6-start and against ef807c1: MISSING 0, DUPLICATE 0 in both. Every CHANGED name against phase6-start appears in the phase doc's "Test moves" table (expected 66 there). Report the count and any name the table lacks; never "fix" a test to reduce it;
- `cargo test --locked architecture` (completion registered) and the terminal_session copy check;
- `cargo check --locked --no-default-features --all-targets`;
- the 6.0a suite 20 times with `cargo test --locked bootstrap::engine_server::tests -- --test-threads=1`; the two inbox tests 50 times by their full paths (`bootstrap::engine_inbox::tests::…`); `cargo test --locked cli::tests::debug_shell_survives_closed_terminal -- --exact`;
- after `cargo build --locked`: `diff <(scripts/hexagonal-refactor/integrations-diff.sh target/hexagonal-refactor/baseline-tree/target/debug/tabsmith) <(scripts/hexagonal-refactor/integrations-diff.sh target/debug/tabsmith)` and the same with precmd-diff.sh are both empty;
- `cargo test --locked --release -- --ignored all_bundle_modules` (1 passed);
- the hand-off facts Phase 7 relies on, by grep (prep7 K1, K5, K6, K11): the marker and the three legacy methods + `llm_history` + `ghost_cache` in bootstrap/engine_server.rs; `send_reply` as the only `Msg::Completion` sender; the twelve 6.0a tests under `bootstrap::engine_server::tests`; `empty_search_term_is_no_prefix_match` in completion/domain/services/suggestion_filter.rs importing from completion/domain/test_fixtures.rs; REGISTERED_MODULES with `completion`, LEGACY_MODULES unchanged;
- report the final test count.
The orchestrator, not you, asks the user for the plan §8 manual smoke (items 1-8, `cargo run -- debug shell zsh` with `TABSMITH_HOME=$(mktemp -d)`): agents cannot drive a terminal. Say in the report that it is due.

No CHANGED test is expected in this step: it edits no test body.

Rules for this step:
- Move code with a script (python slicing by symbol or content, or `git mv` for a whole file), never by retyping it. Diff every moved block against `git show phase6-start:<old file>` (for code an earlier Phase 6 step wrote, against `git show <this step's first parent commit>:<file>`) to prove that only paths, visibility, glossary names and the edits this prompt lists changed.
- New seams are test-first (xp-tdd): RED, GREEN, commit, REFACTOR, commit. New tests use exactly the should_... names this prompt gives. testlock keys tests by fn name, so run `grep -rn "fn <name>(" src` before adding each one: it must be empty. AAA, no mocks (InMemory doubles and real objects only).
- Before every commit, run the full `scripts/hexagonal-refactor/gate.sh` (it must print GATE PASS). Also run `python3 scripts/hexagonal-refactor/testlock.py . phase6-start --diff` and `python3 scripts/hexagonal-refactor/testlock.py . ef807c1 --diff`. MISSING must be 0 and DUPLICATE must be 0 in both (the gate fails only on MISSING against ef807c1; it prints DUPLICATE but does not fail on it). Save the CHANGED list against phase6-start at the start of the step: at every commit it may grow only by the tests this prompt lists as CHANGED. Against ef807c1 many Phase 6 tests were CHANGED before this step, so check only MISSING and DUPLICATE there. Justify every CHANGED test this step adds as a pure restructuring in your report.
- Fitness: from commit 1 on, `completion` is registered for real in src/architecture_tests.rs, and `cargo test --locked architecture` passes in the working tree (the gate runs it). Also at every commit, on a `git archive HEAD | tar -x -C <dir>` copy under target/hexagonal-refactor/review-tmp/, add "terminal_session" to REGISTERED_MODULES and run `cargo test --locked architecture` there (you may point CARGO_TARGET_DIR at a reused directory under target/hexagonal-refactor/review-tmp/, never the main target/). No line may name src/terminal_session/application/ports/; report any other terminal_session line without fixing it (Phase 9 registers that module). Delete the copy.
- Clippy allows 3 warnings, and the baseline already has 3. So no new unused import, unused `mut`, `default_constructed_unit_structs` (build unit structs as `ToggleFuzzySearchUseCase`, never `::default()`), `too_many_arguments` (more than 7 parameters), `large_enum_variant` or other warning. Prune imports as engine.rs shrinks. Never rewrite the run-budget arithmetic with `saturating_*` (GEN-GT9).
- `grep -n 'cfg(windows)\|cfg(unix)\|cfg(all(\|cfg(target_os\|cfg(not(\|cfg!(windows)'` every file you touch. Code under cfg(windows) or cfg(not(unix)) is never compiled here, and a cfg(unix)-only item imported without the same cfg breaks the Windows CI job: check by hand that every path still resolves on both sides.
- Before the step's last commit, `cargo check --locked --no-default-features --all-targets` must pass (the embed-specs feature off).
- Commit as `refactor(completion): <why>` (`test(completion): ...` for a test-only commit). The subject is at most 72 characters: measure it before committing (`printf '%s' "$subject" | wc -m`). Write the message to a file and commit with `git commit -F <file>`: the repo's RTK command hook rewrites words inside `-m` text (it did in Phase 5, f8e6055). Stage explicit paths and end the message with the trailer `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`.
- Never rewrite committed history: no `git commit --amend`, rebase, `git reset` of a commit, `filter-branch` or force. Fix forward with a new commit. A subject over 72 characters is reported, not rewritten.
- `integrations_zsh_powerlevel10k_prompt_wrapped` (shell_integration's embedded_shell_scripts tests) is pty-timing flaky under the gate's parallel load. If it is the gate's only failure, rerun it alone with `cargo test --locked shell_integration::infrastructure::adapters::embedded_shell_scripts::tests::integrations_zsh_powerlevel10k_prompt_wrapped -- --exact` (it must print `1 passed`), then run the full gate again. Never edit, `#[ignore]` or skip it. Any other failing test is a defect of this step.
- Never change behaviour to get green. If you cannot keep it, stop at the last green commit and report.
- The docs commit is `docs(completion): <why>` (Phase 5 precedent: `docs(specs): mark Phase 5 done and record its decisions`), at most 72 characters, with the same trailer and `git commit -F`.
- At the end of this step, after the last commit, run `cargo test --locked --release -- --ignored all_bundle_modules` (plan section 8). It must print `1 passed`; report that line.
- Report: the commits (hash and subject), the final gate lines, both testlock summaries (MISSING, CHANGED, DUPLICATE), every CHANGED test with its justification, the guard runs with their pass counts, every deviation (including the ones this prompt lists), and concerns for later steps.
